          "kind": "record",
          "node": null,
          "title": "<untrusted source=\"repo-docs\">Architecture</untrusted>",
          "text": "<untrusted source=\"repo-docs\">## State\n\n`PaneLayout` (`src/layout/PaneLayout.ts`) is the single source of truth for how a tab's panes are arranged:\nthe split orientation, the panes in order, which pane has focus, and each pane's width in columns. Features\nchange the layout only through the functions in that file.\n</untrusted>",
          "score": 0.016393,
          "why": [
            "rrf:repo-docs#1"
          ],
          "provenance": "deterministic",
          "confirmed": false,
          "trust": "untrusted",
          "cites": [
            "C2"
          ],
          "depth": null,
          "path": null,
          "tokens": 96
        },
        {
          "kind": "record",
          "node": null,
          "title": "<untrusted source=\"repo-docs\">0001: Toggling orientation keeps the focused pane first</untrusted>",
          "text": "<untrusted source=\"repo-docs\"># 0001: Toggling orientation keeps the focused pane first\n\nStatus: accepted (SPL-103)\n\nWhen a person toggles a split between vertical and horizontal, the focused pane becomes the first pane, so the\ncursor stays where the eye already is. Swapping the pane order instead was considered and rejected: it moved the\ncursor to the other side of the screen on every toggle.\n</untrusted>",
          "score": 0.016129,
          "why": [
